    <sys:String x:Key="Instance.Setup.Advanced.PreLaunchCommand.ToolTip">Runs a command or program before Minecraft starts. The global command runs first, followed by this instance’s command. Use Windows Command Prompt syntax.&#x0a;&#x0a;Path tokens (each path ends with \):&#x0a;· {path}: PCL executable folder&#x0a;· {minecraft}: .minecraft folder&#x0a;· {verpath}: Instance folder (.minecraft\versions\instance-name\)&#x0a;· {verindie}: Instance folder when isolation is on; .minecraft folder otherwise&#x0a;· {java}: Java runtime folder&#x0a;&#x0a;Other tokens:&#x0a;· {user}: Player name&#x0a;· {login}: Login method&#x0a;· {uuid}: Player UUID&#x0a;· {name}: Instance name&#x0a;· {date}, {time}: Current system time&#x0a;· {version}: Vanilla version&#x0a;&#x0a;Examples:&#x0a;· &quot;{verpath}test.exe&quot;&#x0a;· &quot;{java}java.exe&quot; -jar &quot;{verpath}test.jar&quot;&#x0a;· notepad &quot;{verindie}options.txt&quot;&#x0a;&#x0a;Put paths in double quotation marks when they may contain spaces. The working directory is the current .minecraft folder.</sys:String>
