    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Title">Telemetry &amp; data collection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Essential.Title">Basic service data (required)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Essential.Intro">The launcher processes the minimum data needed for updates, downloads, security checks, and fault recovery. This cannot be disabled and is never used for advertising or product profiling.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Essential.Items">• Request ID, launcher version/channel, platform/architecture, protocol and API version&#x0a;• Time, status, and network metadata naturally produced by update, download, and online requests you initiate&#x0a;• Security validation outcomes (never tokens)&#x0a;• Critical failure stage, normalized category, and irreversible fingerprint</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Essential.Excludes">We do not upload full exception messages, stacks, breadcrumbs, local paths, launch arguments, log attachments, dumps, account details, or authentication tokens.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Experience.Toggle">Join the User Experience Improvement Program (optional)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Experience.Intro">When enabled, Sentry and PostHog help us find slow operations, unhealthy releases, and workflows that are difficult to complete.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Experience.Items">• Feature usage, page/workflow funnels, and feature flags&#x0a;• Startup, download, game launch, and plugin load performance stages&#x0a;• Cleaned full exceptions, stacks, and limited operation context&#x0a;• Bucketed OS, architecture, runtime, locale, and hardware data</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Oobe.Telemetry.Experience.Withdraw">You can leave at any time in Settings → About &amp; Legal. Leaving immediately stops collection, clears pending data, and deletes the anonymous ID without affecting core features.</sys:String>
